{"id":"20260828T175123.924186927Z-9a6a6083","time":"2026-08-28T17:51:23.924186927Z","session_id":"session-20260828T174912.794794876Z","task_id":"task-1787939352794996084","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  planSource and planDigest each look the supplied plan up separately; make one lookup serve both, with no change in behaviour.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] planSource and planDigest each call suppliedPlan, which locks Engine.mu and reads the same per-task supplied-plan map. (internal/workflow/suppliedplan.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The PlanProposed event and taskContext repeatedly request source and digest for the same task. (internal/workflow/engine.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] A supplied plan is registered before its run begins, and resume restoration re-registers it before deriving the resumed bound. (internal/workflow/suppliedplan.go and internal/workflow/assisted.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Existing supplied-plan tests cover architect-versus-supplied provenance, digest preservation, restart restoration, and fail-closed handling of damaged records. (internal/workflow/suppliedplan_test.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Scoped Sensei preflight classifies the three-file change as architecture-sensitive with local blast radius, no approval gate, sufficient coverage, and six direct critical invariants. (internal/workflow) — source: graph\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: architectural-authority-granted\n"}
{"id":"20260828T175123.924305497Z-1bcb6e3d","time":"2026-08-28T17:51:23.924305497Z","session_id":"session-20260828T174912.794794876Z","task_id":"task-1787939352794996084","source":"architect","kind":"plan.proposed","summary":"Derive supplied-plan source and digest atomically from one lookup while preserving provenance, event, task-context, and resume behavior.\n\nPlan:\n  1. Introduce one source-and-digest lookup and remove the separate accessors.\n  2. Bind the returned pair once when constructing the plan event and task context, then reuse it consistently.\n  3. Update resume handling and existing regression tests to consume and verify the paired result.\n  4. Run gofmt -w cmd internal, go vet ./..., and go test ./....","payload":{"decision":"proceed","summary":"Derive supplied-plan source and digest atomically from one lookup while preserving provenance, event, task-context, and resume behavior.","steps":["Introduce one source-and-digest lookup and remove the separate accessors.","Bind the returned pair once when constructing the plan event and task context, then reuse it consistently.","Update resume handling and existing regression tests to consume and verify the paired result.","Run gofmt -w cmd internal, go vet ./..., and go test ./...."],"consequences":"Supplied-plan provenance is read once per paired use instead of through repeated locked map lookups; architect plans still produce source \"architect\" with an empty digest, supplied plans retain source \"supplied\" with their exact digest, and persisted/resumed bounds remain unchanged.","files":["internal/workflow/suppliedplan.go","internal/workflow/engine.go","internal/workflow/suppliedplan_test.go"],"mode":"modify","related_invariants":["invariant:sensei_code.authority.only_an_explicit_answer_satisfies_a_boundary","invariant:sensei_code.candidate.disposition_is_decided_and_evidence_outlives_removal","invariant:sensei_code.derived.future_only_a_question_cannot_authorize_the_run_that_wrote_it","invariant:sensei_code.workflow.context_never_widens_worker_scope","invariant:sensei_code.workflow.execution_is_authorized_once_at_run","invariant:sensei_code.workflow.repeated_resume_cannot_mint_authority"],"plan":"Replace the separate planSource and planDigest accessors with one helper returning both values from a single supplied-plan lookup. Reuse that pair wherever both values describe the same plan, without changing defaults, emitted records, task context, authority routing, or resume semantics.","claims":[{"statement":"planSource and planDigest each call suppliedPlan, which locks Engine.mu and reads the same per-task supplied-plan map.","about":"internal/workflow/suppliedplan.go","source":"repository"},{"statement":"The PlanProposed event and taskContext repeatedly request source and digest for the same task.","about":"internal/workflow/engine.go","source":"repository"},{"statement":"A supplied plan is registered before its run begins, and resume restoration re-registers it before deriving the resumed bound.","about":"internal/workflow/suppliedplan.go and internal/workflow/assisted.go","source":"repository"},{"statement":"Existing supplied-plan tests cover architect-versus-supplied provenance, digest preservation, restart restoration, and fail-closed handling of damaged records.","about":"internal/workflow/suppliedplan_test.go","source":"repository"},{"statement":"Scoped Sensei preflight classifies the three-file change as architecture-sensitive with local blast radius, no approval gate, sufficient coverage, and six direct critical invariants.","about":"internal/workflow","source":"graph"}],"plan_source":"architect"}}
