{"id":"20260828T175212.910466577Z-1ba45d7a","time":"2026-08-28T17:52:12.910466577Z","session_id":"session-20260828T174912.794794876Z","task_id":"task-1787939352794996084","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeVa8isTeBV7BVwjM2W4P\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Done — committed on the candidate branch.\\n\\n**What changed**\\n- `internal/workflow/suppliedplan.go`: replaced `planSource` and `planDigest` with one `planProvenance(taskID) (PlanSource, string)` that does a single `suppliedPlan` lookup and returns `(PlanSupplied, digest)` or `(PlanByArchitect, \\\"\\\")` — same values as before. `restorePlanBound` binds the source from it (digest discarded there, as before).\\n- `internal/workflow/engine.go:695`: the pair is bound once (`planSource, planDigest := e.planProvenance(taskID)`) and reused for the `PlanProposed` event source, summary, `proposedPlan` payload, and `taskContext` — replacing five separate lookups.\\n- `internal/workflow/suppliedplan_test.go`: the three assertions now consume the pair and also check the digest (present for supplied, empty for architect/refused-resume). Package and imports unchanged, per the edit grant.\\n\\n**Verification**\\n- `gofmt -w cmd internal`, `go vet ./...` clean.\\n- `go test ./...` passes everywhere except `internal/publish TestCommitAndPushReachARealRemote`, which fails with `sensei-code: push is refused; publication is human-owned` — the worker session's push guard blocking the test's push to a temp remote. Environmental, not caused by this change.\\n\\nNothing outside the plan was touched; no Sensei knowledge proposed since no bug was fixed.\\n\\nAWG: briefing(internal/workflow/engine.go) | invariants: plan source/digest always describe the same plan; resume never changes plan authorship | uncertainty: publish push test blocked by worker guard, not re-verifiable here\"}],\"