{"id":"20260828T175420.073146703Z-7e104f97","time":"2026-08-28T17:54:20.073146703Z","session_id":"session-20260828T174912.794794876Z","task_id":"task-1787939352794996084","source":"reviewer","kind":"output","summary":"{\"decision\":\"revise\",\"summary\":\"The event path correctly binds source and digest once, but the resume path still splits the provenance pair. Sensei’s authoritative preflight marks this architecture-sensitive and requires that “Resume revalidates recorded authority and never mints new authority”; the supplied audit PASS does not prove the required resume binding.\",\"instructions\":\"Extend resumedBound to carry PlanDigest. In restorePlanBound, bind `source, digest := e.planProvenance(task.TaskID)` and return both. Construct resumed taskContext from `bound.Source` and `bound.PlanDigest`, not `task.PlanDigest`. Update resume regression coverage to assert the restored paired digest equals p.Digest and reaches the resumed task context/reviewer packet.\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"f1\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"claim\":\"Resume provenance now consumes the paired lookup.\",\"reference\":\"internal/workflow/suppliedplan.go:191; internal/workflow/engine.go:3804\",\"reason\":\"restorePlanBound discards the lookup digest (`source, _`), while the resumed task context takes its digest separately from task.PlanDigest. Thus source and digest are not bound and reused as one pair on resume, contrary to the architectural plan. Sensei’s active critical invariant says “Resume revalidates recorded authority and never mints new authority”; provenance used by the resumed worker must remain one re-established identity.\",\"correction\":\"Carry the digest in resumedBound, bind both values from planProvenance once after restoration, and use that pair to populate resumed taskContext.\",\"proof_gap\":\"TestASuppliedPlanSurvivesResumeOrFailsClosed only asserts that the helper digest is non-empty; it does not prove equality with p.Digest or that the resumed task context/reviewer packet uses the restored pair.\"}]}","payload":{"stream":"stderr"}}
