{"id":"20260828T180226.795801233Z-faf1dd07","time":"2026-08-28T18:02:26.795801233Z","session_id":"session-20260828T174912.794794876Z","task_id":"task-1787939352794996084","source":"codex","kind":"output","summary":"docs/architecture.md:100:Governed mode is the autonomous orchestrated pipeline described in the rest of this document: isolated candidate worktrees, bounded workers, deterministic diff audit, reviewer cycles, Sensei admission, exact-artifact apply, verification, and terminal completion.","payload":{"stream":"stderr"}}
{"id":"20260828T180226.795823003Z-c1e44ab3","time":"2026-08-28T18:02:26.795823003Z","session_id":"session-20260828T174912.794794876Z","task_id":"task-1787939352794996084","source":"codex","kind":"output","summary":"docs/architecture.md:106:A task is governed because the canonical Sensei task, candidate, admission, verification, and completion records exist for it — not because a config key says `governed`.","payload":{"stream":"stderr"}}
{"id":"20260828T180226.795840115Z-98eb4f5f","time":"2026-08-28T18:02:26.795840115Z","session_id":"session-20260828T174912.794794876Z","task_id":"task-1787939352794996084","source":"codex","kind":"output","summary":"docs/architecture.md:114:This is deliberate and evidence-based. In Sensei's own grpc-go comparison, an agent working with Sensei context solved 3/3 tasks while the governed synthesis driver produced 1/3 candidates, and both of its failures were the O3 whole-file-rewrite protocol failing to scale (a 128KB snapshot), not a reasoning failure. The R1 pilot showed the same ordering at larger n (9/9 against 5/9).","payload":{"stream":"stderr"}}
{"id":"20260828T180226.795860933Z-6e5a13c4","time":"2026-08-28T18:02:26.795860933Z","session_id":"session-20260828T174912.794794876Z","task_id":"task-1787939352794996084","source":"codex","kind":"output","summary":"docs/architecture.md:116:The counter-evidence is preserved rather than discarded: the single candidate the synthesis driver did produce was the *more disciplined* repair — one file and four lines against the real feature flag, where the agent's accepted solve touched three files and deleted roughly a hundred test helpers. Generation quality is not the reason O3 is out of the path; protocol scaling is. If that scaling problem is solved upstream, this decision should be revisited on the evidence.","payload":{"stream":"stderr"}}
{"id":"20260828T180226.795888224Z-88ddd2f2","time":"2026-08-28T18:02:26.795888224Z","session_id":"session-20260828T174912.794794876Z","task_id":"task-1787939352794996084","source":"codex","kind":"output","summary":"docs/architecture.md:118:What Sensei Code **does** use, in governed mode, are Sensei's evaluation, admission, verification, and closure owners — applied to an agent-produced candidate.","payload":{"stream":"stderr"}}
{"id":"20260828T180226.795909322Z-7acf5019","time":"2026-08-28T18:02:26.795909322Z","session_id":"session-20260828T174912.794794876Z","task_id":"task-1787939352794996084","source":"codex","kind":"output","summary":"docs/architecture.md:122:Sensei's candidate evaluation and admission owners were built around candidates that Sensei's own driver generated. Whether they accept an **externally generated** candidate — an agent-produced worktree diff sealed by Sensei Code — is an open contract question against Sensei core, not a settled integration.","payload":{"stream":"stderr"}}
{"id":"20260828T180226.795938025Z-ae39c059","time":"2026-08-28T18:02:26.795938025Z","session_id":"session-20260828T174912.794794876Z","task_id":"task-1787939352794996084","source":"codex","kind":"output","summary":"docs/architecture.md:124:It must be resolved before governed mode can be called complete. Until it is resolved, governed mode terminates at *candidate ready for governed admission*, which is the fail-closed boundary already described in section 15. Sensei Code must not invent a local candidate artifact format to route around the question.","payload":{"stream":"stderr"}}
