{"id":"20260828T180226.800838963Z-6bdec5e0","time":"2026-08-28T18:02:26.800838963Z","session_id":"session-20260828T174912.794794876Z","task_id":"task-1787939352794996084","source":"codex","kind":"output","summary":"docs/awareness/invariants.yaml:176:    description: \"Admission evaluates a convergence bundle, which is Sensei's synthesis output; composing something bundle-shaped locally would produce records that satisfy the schema and mean nothing. So Sensei Code builds argv for synthesis-admit, admit-change, synthesis-apply and verify-admission, wires each step to what the previous one wrote, and reads exit codes — it decides nothing. Only admit-change establishes admission: reviewer acceptance does not, a passing diff audit does not, and a chain that ran without error does not. Admission is permission to attempt rather than proof of correctness, and scope compliance is not correctness certification. A refusal is distinguished from a broken toolchain, and an exit code this build does not recognise is reported as unrecognised rather than mapped onto an existing meaning.\"","payload":{"stream":"stderr"}}
