{"id":"20260828T180226.800931754Z-eb433744","time":"2026-08-28T18:02:26.800931754Z","session_id":"session-20260828T174912.794794876Z","task_id":"task-1787939352794996084","source":"codex","kind":"output","summary":"docs/awareness/invariants.yaml:192:    description: \"Every governed task creates a worktree and a branch, and a candidate nobody resolved means nothing in particular — which turns recovery from disk into archaeology and erodes the value of an exact persisted base. So each candidate reaches a stated disposition from a closed vocabulary, retention carries the reason that kept it, and nothing is removed before its base, diff and audit evidence are written down. Automatic removal is reached only by a candidate whose own recorded evidence says it holds no work: deleting on exit would perform the deletion half of a publication decision the system correctly refuses to make.\"","payload":{"stream":"stderr"}}
