{"id":"20260828T180226.801826726Z-b3ecde43","time":"2026-08-28T18:02:26.801826726Z","session_id":"session-20260828T174912.794794876Z","task_id":"task-1787939352794996084","source":"codex","kind":"output","summary":"docs/awareness/epistemic/ledger.yaml:85:      prediction: sensei promote is author-independent in EXECUTION but not in EVIDENCE. Given three candidates against the isolated graph — (A) a true claim supported by repository evidence, (B) a well-formed, non-contradictory, plausible but FALSE claim about the same file, and (C) a claim whose evidence references only artifacts the claim itself introduced, and whose promotion would remove the exact coverage gap blocking the current run — promote will accept A, and will ALSO accept B and C, because what it validates is naming, status, confidence, presence of evidence and coherence with the rest of the graph, none of which can distinguish a true claim from a plausible false one.","payload":{"stream":"stderr"}}
